{"text": "WILLIAM S. MCKERSIE, PHD\n\nPROFILE.\n\nSenior educational leader skilled in promoting excellence in elementary and secondary education to\ncensure success for all students. Known for leading collaboration among school boards and committees,\nteacher unions, teachers, principals, community leaders, business leaders, parents and students in urban\nand suburban communities. Seasoned team leader with exceptional policy, political, management,\ncommunication and budget oversight skills.\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\n\nASSOCIATE SUPERINTENDENT FOR ACADEMIC EXCELLENCE 2008-Present\nArchdiocese of Boston, Braintree, MA\n'* Provide strategic direction and service to promote academic excellence for all 122 elementary and\nsecondary schools (serving 42,000 students) within the Archdiocese of Boston. Priorities include\nadoption of Massachusetts Common Core, aligned curriculum frameworks and instructional plans;\ntechnology integration; evidence-based decision making; comprehensive, multiple measure system.\nfor tracking school and student achievement and growth; multi-faceted professional development\nprogram for principals and teachers; and hiring and evaluation of principals.\n\nPEER REVIEWER, RACE TO THE TOP GRANT COMPETITION\nUnited States Department of Education, Washington, DC 2010\n\u2018* Served as one of 70 nationally-selected peer reviewers for the first and second rounds of the Race to\nthe Top Grant Competition, 2010. Selected to chair state finalist interviews in both rounds.\n\nASSOCIATE DEAN FOR DEVELOPMENT & ALUMNI RELATIONS 2004-2008\nHarvard Graduate School of Education, Cambridge, MA\n\u2018* Directed a 17-member division dedicated to helping alumni and friends of the Ed School \u201cgive\nthrough\u201d Harvard to have far-reaching impact on educational research, leadership, and policymaking.\nSecured over $30 million dollars in gifts and pledges. Captured the school\u2019s largest gift in history\n(si2 .), two professorships ($3 million apiece), and major financial aid support ($4.2 million).\nOversaw an annual budget of nearly $2 million, Member of Dean\u2019s Cabinet.\n\nDIRECTOR, HIGH SCHOOL TRANSFORMATION INITIATIVE, 2002-2004\nCleveland Heights-University Heights Public Schools, Cleveland Heights, OH\n\u2018* Directed transformation of 2,200 student urban high school into five small schools. Process involved\nover 80 individuals\u2014board members, superintendent, district administrators, principals, teacher\nleaders, teachers, union officials, students, parents and community members. Cleveland Heights,\nHigh was one of 20 urban high schools in Ohio in a statewide initiative funded by the Bill and\nMelinda Gates Foundation in partnership with the Knowledge Works Foundation,\n\n\u2018SENIOR PROGRAM OFFICER FOR EDUCATION 1997-2002\n\u2018The Cleveland Foundation, Cleveland, OH\n\u2018* Directed all K-12 and higher education leadership and grant making. Awarded over $27 million in\ngrants. Worked with public and private board to develop and implement education strategy focused on\npublic school reform in Greater Cleveland. Supported strategic level change in Catholic schools.\nCollaborated with school district, teachers union, nonprofit, civic, municipal, and business leaders to\nestablish school reform priorities and identify philanthropic support.",
